grammar Ll1PlusPrefixConflict

// The Plus loop matches its continuation greedily. The continuation FIRST set
// {"a"} and the follow of the loop {"ab"} are disjoint as identities, so the
// Plus was classified LL(1). But "a" is a prefix of "ab", so on input `aab`
// the loop consumes "a" twice, eating the "a" that should start "ab", then
// "ab" fails on the trailing "b". The only valid parse takes one "a", then
// "ab". A sound classifier routes the Plus through GLL. This is the case the
// directional guard already caught: the continuation terminal prefixes the
// follow terminal.
S = "a"+ "ab"
